{"id": "sevt_01Aexyr7z71jQrLTJnAVjumR", "content": [{"text": "The checkout deploy at 14:46:05 caused the spike. It replaced one batched query with a query per order row (an N+1).\n\n- **Timing:** Checkout deploy `ccf7a0f` went out at 14:46:05. Checkout p99 was about 70\u201380 ms until 14:45. It was 3006 ms at 14:46 and 3.2\u20134.3 s from then on. The cart (14:18) and inventory (12:20) deploys are too early to line up.\n- **Diff:** The commit is labelled \"refactor for readability\". It removed the single `OrderItem ... order_id__in=ids` query that grouped results in memory. In its place, `build_summary` now runs `OrderItem.objects.filter(order_id=...)` once per open order inside a loop.\n- **Log:** The per-row query `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id = ?` appears 1,555 times, starting at 14:46:08 on checkout-1. A single request, `req_10fe9ddc8c77`, issues many of them back to back. The batched `order_id IN` form appears 201 times in the log. I didn't check when those 201 occurred, but the batched query was presumably the pre-deploy path.\n\nI didn't check `db_pool_utilization`, because a deploy lined up and the runbook only calls for it when none does. Revert `ccf7a0f`, or restore the batched query.\n\n> **Root cause:** `ccf7a0f` \u2014 the \"readability\" refactor of `CheckoutSummaryHandler.build_summary` replaced one batched `order_id IN (...)` query with a per-order query in a loop (N+1), so checkout p99 went from about 75 ms to over 3 s.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T05:45:22.353223Z", "type": "agent.message"}
